# Day 5: Linux logs
## What I Learned
- Linux logs  can be read with journalctl (or /var/log/auth.log)
- "password check failed" = failed login, "session opened for user root" = succesful sudo
- Same logic as Windows: failed logins (4625), then succes (4624)

## What I did
- Typed a wrong sudo password 3 times on my own Kali machine
- Read the logs with journalctl and found 3 "password check failed" lines and the "3 incorrect password attemps" line
- Found the succesful sudo session after I used the correct password
- Saw CRON entries and recognized them as normal system activity
